<title>CANADA: StatsCan survey sees Feb unemployment at 9.7 pct.</title>
<headline>StatsCan survey sees Feb unemployment at 9.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Statistics Canada survey of analysts forecast Canadian unemployment remaining flat in February from January at 9.7 percent.</p>
<p>The survey also forecast that consumer prices would rise in February by 2.1 percent from a year earlier.</p>
<p>The survey forecast gross domestic product to rise 0.2 percent in January from December.</p>
<p>The economists also forecast merchandise exports for February at C$22.4 billion, and imports of C$20.3 billion.</p>
<p>The agency on average surveys 17 economists each month.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau, 613-235-6745))</p>
<p>	     -</p>
